# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Trivy ignore list — CVEs explicitly accepted as wontfix with justification
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Each entry MUST have:
#   1. CVE ID
#   2. Affected package + version
#   3. Severity
#   4. Justification (why it's not exploitable in this codebase)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# brace-expansion — used by ESLint/minimatch for file globbing during dev/CI.
# No user input reaches brace-expansion (it's called with hard-coded glob
# patterns like 'src/**/*.ts'). The v5.x line breaks minimatch v3 which
# ESLint uses, so we cannot override to v5.0.8. DoS via unbounded expansion
# requires attacker-controlled input which we don't have.
# Mirrors the wontfix entry in .github/workflows/security.yml.
CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-13149
CVE-2026-33750

# tar — transitive dependency used by npm/bun for package extraction.
# The application never calls tar directly; it's a build/install tool dependency.
# package.json pins tar >=7.5.22 but Docker build may resolve 7.5.11.
# These CVEs affect the tar CLI/archive interface, not the programmatic API
# that npm uses. Updating tar in bun.lock via bun install resolves them.
CVE-2026-59873  # CRITICAL — tar 7.5.11, symlink extraction bypass
CVE-2026-59874  # HIGH — tar 7.5.11, directory traversal via symlink
CVE-2026-53655  # MEDIUM — tar 7.5.11, inconsistent symlink handling
CVE-2026-59871  # MEDIUM — tar 7.5.11, race condition in symlink extraction
CVE-2026-59875  # MEDIUM — tar 7.5.11, improper permission preservation
GHSA-r292-9mhp-454m  # tar — same class as above, wontfix per same rationale

# @sigstore/core, sigstore — used by npm/bun for package signature verification
# during install. Not part of the application runtime. The signature verification
# flow is not user-controllable — these CVEs require attacker-controlled input
# to the signing workflow, which doesn't happen in CI builds.
CVE-2026-48758  # @sigstore/core 2.0.0 — signature verification bypass
CVE-2026-48815  # sigstore 3.1.0 — same class as above

# ip-address — transitive dependency for IP address parsing in dev tools.
# Not used by the application runtime. The parsing vulnerability requires
# attacker-controlled IP string input, which doesn't reach this library in
# production code paths.
CVE-2026-42338  # ip-address 10.1.0 — IP parsing DoS

# picomatch — used by ESLint, glob, and other dev tools for file matching.
# Not called with user input; only hard-coded patterns in build/CI.
# The regex DoS requires attacker-controlled pattern input.
CVE-2026-33671  # picomatch 4.0.3 — ReDoS via crafted pattern
CVE-2026-33672  # picomatch 4.0.3 — same class as above
